      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find the integral of ${(8-\\frac{5}{x})}^{2}$ with respect to $x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Expanding the binomial and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(8-\\frac{5}{x})}^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int (64-\\frac{80}{x}+\\frac{25}{{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 64\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{80}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{25}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =64\\int \\text{d}x-80\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+25\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =64x-80\\ln|x|+25\\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{-2+1}+C \\\\  & =64x-80\\ln|x|-\\frac{25}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
